==============================================================================
N04c_equilibrium_long: the registered equilibrium follow-up (T = 200)
EVIDENCE ONLY: simulations are numerical evidence, not proofs.
finite-N Galerkin truncation evidence: ODE system, always regular at fixed N; NOT a singularity claim; the question is equilibrium vs continuing pump at fixed truncation
==============================================================================
Galerkin runs: n = 32, nu = 0.02, dt = 0.004 (doubled vs N04b), T = 200.0 = 50000 steps/run, A = 1.0, seed = 7; dealiased 2/3 rule (cutoff k_max = 10.67); snapshots every 25 steps (delta = 0.1); viscous time at the forcing scale 1/(nu*k_f^2) = 50: T = 4x it.
Runs: classical (no drag), a0cap (capped dry drag |d| <= 0.02). cd-0.3 skipped (already equilibrated in N04b).
  [classical] step 10000/50000 (20%) elapsed 238 s
  [classical] step 20000/50000 (40%) elapsed 465 s
  [classical] step 30000/50000 (60%) elapsed 696 s
  [classical] step 40000/50000 (80%) elapsed 931 s
